{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>From the voice of</b> — the sense is: his voice is upon me." "<b>distress of</b> — as in its Targum: trouble that comes upon me from the wicked. And some say: it is from the root of כאשר תעיק." "<b>they bring down</b> — from the root of ומטה ידו עמך, and it is from the heavy stem, and the [corresponding] active [form] is אזן."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 55, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:31:58.210367446Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}